## Review1 corrections — implemented, independent re-review pending

Initial independent review requested changes; this checkpoint repairs the three specific blockers without product execution. `va_review1_fix.diff` is the literal incremental diff against `replay_va.py.before_review1`; full proposed code+data remain in `va_adapter_literal.diff`. The reviewed bootstrap guard/data are unchanged.

Each case now saves a separate atomic `out/cases/NNNN.json` BEFORE the next case starts, followed by aggregate results. It retains bounded literal product return/refusal text and known-exception diagnostic (4096 characters each, original length, full SHA256 and truncation flag), rendered command/argv, classifier, exact product event payloads plus global index range, all alias-specific historical expectations/findings/method changes, and snapshot/adapter/data identity. Invalid/superseded cases retain explicit NOT_RUN status and mappings. Aggregate event loss on interruption cannot erase an already completed case's primitive evidence. Writes are confined to validated scratch root; no real credential content is used.

Before EVERY runnable product case, a matched RAW recorder-only control invokes installed `subprocess.run` with exactly the same rebased argv. It must raise ReplayBlocked, record EXACTLY ONE subprocess event matching every argv token hash, and leave marker absent. No recorder replacement, saved original, executable/network fallback or semantic/executable-availability claim is introduced. The control's exact events/range/status are persisted with that case. Control failure is persisted and aborts before product invocation. Every product PASS therefore carries its same-input recorder evidence; the global canaries remain supplementary.

Product cases permit zero or one subprocess event. Any duplicate attempt fails as FAIL_MULTIPLE_PRIMITIVE_ATTEMPTS and aborts after retaining evidence; nonmatching primitive/argv or integrity/marker failure likewise saves failure then aborts. Positive controls and observed residuals require exactly one event. Refusal cases still fail on any event, even alongside [BLOCKED] output. Pure tests additionally validate duplicate/wrong-input rejection, merged alias provenance, literal truncation and missing approval gate. These tests exercise data/helpers only: NO target import, recorder installation, historical probe or product canary was run. Final frozen-source graph refresh and independent corrected-adapter approval remain required before coordinator authorization.

